# L1 checkpoints (consumer-owned)

When `checkpoints.enabled` is true in `.overseer/config.yaml`:

1. Define steps in consumer `policy/checkpoints.yaml` (not in the kit).
2. Run `overseer verify-step` before advancing work — do not hand-edit `verified: true`.
3. Keep verify scripts repo-relative, executable, and exit `0` only with proof.

The kit orchestrates; your domain pack decides what “pass” means.
